Right-hand side: f(f(a + b)) = f(2(a + b) + d) = 2*(2(a + b) + d) + d = 4(a + b) + 2d + d = 4a + 4b + 3d.

Yes, that matches. So, f(a) = 2a + d is indeed a solution for any integer d.

Now, what about c = 0? Then f(a) = d, a constant function.

Plug into the equation: f(2a) + 2f(b) = d + 2d = 3d.

On the right-hand side: f(f(a + b)) = f(d) = d.

So, 3d = d => 2d = 0 => d = 0.

