### Criteria for an upper bound on the degree of an affine variety

We provide criteria to establish an upper bound on the degree of an affine variety in terms of
the product of the degrees of its defining polynomials. The key result is `norm_cast_small` which
gives a bound on the norm of an element of an algebraic number field in terms of its minimal polynomial
and possibly `roots_of_unity` to handle cases where the element is a root of unity.

The norm is crucial in `Hasse's theorem` on the degree of an affine variety, so we include `norm_cast_small`
as an immediate corollary since the product of the degrees of an affine variety is the norm of the ideal
of all its interpolating polynomials.
